# Update app context memory

After substantive changes to how Duality works, update long-term context **in the same turn** (do not wait to be asked).

## When to update

Update if you changed any of:

- Physics / bounce / territory capture / reset / headless engine
- Shaders (`light` / `collision` / `reflection`), glow, trails, frontier, bleed
- `GfxOptions` / `ShaderConfig` / themes / defaults
- Sessions, settings persistence, API runs, DB schema
- New modules or moved file responsibilities
- Renderer backend (Canvas 2D / Pixi)

Skip for pure typo/CSS polish, unrelated refactors, or docs-only edits.

## What to update

1. `docs/APP_CONTEXT.md` (source of truth in repo)
2. Mirror the same file to agent stores when writable:
   - `…/c4a5f014-e556-461e-847d-9ec0622fc505/files/duality-2.0-context.md`
   - `…/u313789205/files/duality-2.0-context.md`

Bump the “Aktualizováno” date. Edit only the sections that changed — keep the doc accurate and concise.

## Habit

If the session touched sim/render/shader/API and you are about to stop, quickly check whether `docs/APP_CONTEXT.md` still matches reality; if not, patch it before finishing.
